0,Eastern Bolivian Guaraní language - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern_Bolivian_Guaraní_language,"Eastern Bolivian Guaraní, known locally as Chawuncu or Chiriguano (pejorative), is a Guaraní language spoken in South America. In Bolivia 33,670 speakers, called the Ava Guaraní people were counted in the year 2000, in the south-central Parapeti River area and in the city of Tarija. [2]","Guaraní, Eastern Bolivian",Tupian
1,Guaraní people - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guaraní_people,"Eastern Bolivian Guaraní The Guaraní people in Bolivia, called Chiriguanos, lived in the foothills of the Andes and had a different history than most other Guaraní people.","Guaraní, Eastern Bolivian",Tupian
